WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.275 --> 00:00:03.746
- We gotta knead with perseverance.

00:00:03.746 --> 00:00:07.333
Don't give up all because it's
gonna be delicious, trust me.

00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:09.750
(calm music)

00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:14.705
Hey, guys, I'm Brenda,
I'm a Tasty producer.

00:00:14.705 --> 00:00:18.658
I will be testing homemade
versus store-bought pasta.

00:00:18.658 --> 00:00:22.179
I need to know is it worth
taking the extra time,

00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:25.395
the extra effort to
make pasta from scratch?

00:00:25.395 --> 00:00:27.026
Is it even better?

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.949
'Cause if it's not better, come on.

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:32.256
So I'm just gonna get cooking in here

00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:36.173
and you and I will take
this journey right now.

00:00:38.176 --> 00:00:40.282
My first impression of homemade pasta

00:00:40.282 --> 00:00:44.170
was does it really take just
flour and eggs to make this?

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.331
I mean, come on,

00:00:45.331 --> 00:00:48.064
everybody has these two
ingredients at home.

00:00:48.064 --> 00:00:50.564
The process, also very simple.

00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:55.220
You make your flour volcano,
you gradually add eggs

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.936
and then you begin mixing.

00:00:56.936 --> 00:00:59.353
(calm music)

00:01:08.228 --> 00:01:10.460
So don't be afraid of
getting your hands dirty.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.089
This is what happens
when you play with dough.

00:01:13.089 --> 00:01:15.776
Think of yourselves as a kitten

00:01:15.776 --> 00:01:18.596
who happens to look like Ed Sheeran.

00:01:18.596 --> 00:01:19.429
I mean, think about it.

00:01:19.429 --> 00:01:22.193
Ed Sheeran does look like a kitten

00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:24.292
and this kitten meaning you,

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:27.586
you depend on your
kneading skills to survive.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.553
You know when kittens
give little massages?

00:01:29.553 --> 00:01:30.934
This is what it is, it's kneading

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:34.351
and this is what we need to do well today

00:01:35.643 --> 00:01:37.893
to get amazing pasta dough.

00:01:42.195 --> 00:01:46.012
The entire process takes me
around one hour and a half.

00:01:46.012 --> 00:01:47.919
That includes mixing ingredients,

00:01:47.919 --> 00:01:52.691
resting the dough, flattening,
cutting, shaping your dough.

00:01:52.691 --> 00:01:56.096
However, it's not a complicated process.

00:01:56.096 --> 00:01:59.596
On the contrary, it's pretty entertaining.

00:02:03.449 --> 00:02:06.288
This is an 80 something dollar machine

00:02:06.288 --> 00:02:08.733
but you can get one for around $30

00:02:08.733 --> 00:02:11.179
and it'll get the job done.

00:02:11.179 --> 00:02:15.006
You don't need it, you can
do this entire thing by hand

00:02:15.006 --> 00:02:17.796
but trust me, this will
make your job smoother

00:02:17.796 --> 00:02:19.379
and a lot more fun.

00:02:20.696 --> 00:02:21.993
So here's the thing.

00:02:21.993 --> 00:02:24.538
Every time you run the
dough through the machine,

00:02:24.538 --> 00:02:27.572
you wanna increase these
little numbers right here

00:02:27.572 --> 00:02:31.064
and the higher they go, the
thinner the dough will get.

00:02:31.064 --> 00:02:34.530
I realized that seven is my ideal number

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.433
but a good way to guide yourself

00:02:36.433 --> 00:02:39.843
is to stop when you see your
fingers through the dough.

00:02:39.843 --> 00:02:42.260
(calm music)

00:02:52.525 --> 00:02:55.170
Alright, so it comes down
to the store-bought version

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.724
and we have right here
fettuccine from the box.

00:02:57.724 --> 00:02:59.779
The difference is evident.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:02.589
This is thicker, it's no longer flowy

00:03:02.589 --> 00:03:06.756
and as far as I understand,
there are no eggs in here.

00:03:16.365 --> 00:03:19.662
You can serve your fettuccine
with any pasta sauce

00:03:19.662 --> 00:03:21.609
but with thick Alfredo sauce

00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:24.942
really highlights the
properties of fettuccine

00:03:24.942 --> 00:03:26.609
especially homemade.

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:37.734
Alright, let's break this down.

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:40.637
In terms of price, the
store-bought is the winner.

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:43.194
Time, store-bought wins again.

00:03:43.194 --> 00:03:47.957
Texture, the homemade version,
it's silkier, it's smoother.

00:03:47.957 --> 00:03:51.251
In terms of preparation, this
is very straight to the point.

00:03:51.251 --> 00:03:53.439
You open the box, you
put it in boiling water

00:03:53.439 --> 00:03:55.552
and blah, blah, blah,
you know how it goes.

00:03:55.552 --> 00:03:57.711
Here, you're gonna have some fun.

00:03:57.711 --> 00:04:01.731
When I say it's like Play-Doh
for grown ups, I am not lying.

00:04:01.731 --> 00:04:04.254
Now, I also asked people on Instagram

00:04:04.254 --> 00:04:08.421
based on looks, they would go
100% for the homemade version

00:04:09.656 --> 00:04:11.354
and I have to agree with them.

00:04:11.354 --> 00:04:13.648
You're gonna love it and I guarantee it.

00:04:13.648 --> 00:04:17.088
Besides, the flavor, a
thousand times better.

00:04:17.088 --> 00:04:20.372
I mean, three out of my
three testers agree with me.

00:04:20.372 --> 00:04:23.228
You're really gonna love it.

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:24.061
Mm.

00:04:25.105 --> 00:04:25.938
Oh my God.

00:04:26.887 --> 00:04:28.495
It's just so good.

00:04:28.495 --> 00:04:29.549
I'm out of here.

00:04:29.549 --> 00:04:30.789
Have a good day.

00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:33.206
(calm music)

